    // At the start of second T, Yang's HP is HP_initial - dmgM*(T-1).
    // During second T, Yang's HP decreases by dmgM.
    // But the condition is: Once monster's HP <= 0 AND Yang's HP > 0.
    // The decreases happen simultaneously.
    // So at the end of second T, Monster HP <= 0.
    // Yang's HP at end of second T is HP_initial - dmgM * T.
    // Wait, the problem says "Once monster's HP <= 0 and the same time Master Yang's HP > 0".
    // This implies we check the state after the simultaneous decrease.
    // So we need HP_initial - dmgM * T > 0.
    // Therefore, HP_initial > dmgM * T.
